-- title:
--   Unipotent flat local bound: dim H¹_f ≤ h⁰ + 1
-- statement:
--   Let $k$ be a finite field, $p$ an odd prime with $k$ of characteristic $p$, and fix an algebra structure $\mathbb{Z}_p \to \mathbb{Z}/p$ whose kernel is the ideal generated by $p$. Let $\bar\rho$ be a residual Galois representation over $k$, that is, a $k$-vector space $V$ with $\dim_k V = 2$ together with a monoid homomorphism $\rho$ from $\mathrm{Gal}(\overline{\mathbb{Q}}/\mathbb{Q})$ to $\mathrm{End}_k(V)$ which is trivial on the automorphisms fixing some finite-dimensional intermediate field. Assume the unipotent flatness hypothesis `hunip`: there is a commutative ring $H$ carrying a Hopf algebra structure over $\mathbb{Z}_p$, finite and flat as a $\mathbb{Z}_p$-module and with cocommutative comultiplication, such that the Cartier dual (the $\mathbb{Z}/p$-linear dual) of $\mathbb{Z}/p \otimes_{\mathbb{Z}_p} H$ is a local ring, and there is a bijection $e$ from the convolution group `WithConv` of $\mathbb{Z}_p$-algebra maps $H \to$ `PadicAlgCl p` onto $V \times V$ which carries convolution products to sums and which intertwines the action of the local Galois group $\mathrm{Aut}_{\mathbb{Q}_p}(\overline{\mathbb{Q}}_p)$ on points with the untwisted (zero cocycle) action `dualLiftModuleActAd p 0`, i.e. the diagonal action of $\rho$ composed with the restriction map to the global Galois group. The conclusion is twofold: the submodule `localFlatClassesAd p`, namely the $k$-span inside $H^1$ of the restriction to the local group of the adjoint representation $\sigma \mapsto (f \mapsto \rho(\sigma) f \rho(\sigma^{-1}))$ of the classes of those $1$-cocycles $c$ admitting such a finite flat cocommutative Hopf algebra model with $e$ equivariant for the $c$-twisted action `dualLiftModuleActAd p c`, is finite-dimensional over $k$; and its dimension is at most $\dim_k$ of the invariants of the restricted adjoint representation, plus $1$.
--
--   This is the local bound at $p$ for the flat deformation condition, $\dim_k H^1_f(\mathbb{Q}_p, \mathrm{ad}\,\bar\rho) \le \dim_k H^0(\mathbb{Q}_p, \mathrm{ad}\,\bar\rho) + 1$, in the case where the given finite flat Hopf algebra model has unipotent special fibre (Cartier dual local), which is the case handled by the unipotent Dieudonné/Honda-system formalism. It feeds the general flat local bound [`ResidualGaloisRep.finiteDimensional_localFlatClassesAd_and_finrank_le`](thm.html#ResidualGaloisRep.finiteDimensional_localFlatClassesAd_and_finrank_le) and its base-change variant.
